    {
      "id": "VIS-001",
      "severity": "release-blocking",
      "title": "Reference-faithful geometry remains unproven",
      "finding": "The regeneration now preserves varied authored primitives: 268 boxes, 48 cylinders, 78 decks, 44 chamfered boxes and 21 hull components. This fixes the previous all-box manifest finding, but the visual fleet still repeats a simplified slab-hull/template vocabulary and all 20 synchronized quality records fail distinctive-features. Model-specific hull, glazing, roofline and deck treatment are not sufficiently resolved for release.",
      "requiredAction": "Refine each hull and superstructure against its selected references, preserve the authored non-box semantics in exports, and repeat the distinctive-feature review."
    },
    {
      "id": "VIS-002",
      "severity": "release-blocking",
      "title": "Rooms remain blockout assemblies",
      "finding": "All 111 room records have canonical evidence, but the visual review still shows beds, partitions, benches, cylinders and simple equipment blocks without complete room shells, joinery, fixtures, machinery, support relationships or seam closure. Superhawk rooms are now visible on the corrected canonical paths, but remain close-up primitive assemblies. The synchronized records fail furnished-rooms, no-intersections, no-floating-fittings, closed-seams and physical-supports for every yacht.",
      "requiredAction": "Complete the room architecture and model-specific fixtures/equipment, resolve support and intersection relationships, and regenerate the canonical room evidence."
    },
    {
      "id": "VIS-003",
      "severity": "release-blocking",
      "title": "Material fidelity is not release quality",
      "finding": "All 84 GLBs now contain materials, textures and images, with 626 records of each kind; the embedded images are all 32x32 PNGs. This passes payload presence but not visual material quality. The canonical renders remain largely flat color blocks and the synchronized quality records fail textures and materials-in-all-views on all 20 yachts.",
      "requiredAction": "Use sufficiently resolved, model-appropriate material treatment and demonstrate legible, consistent materials in every required canonical view, then rerun the quality checks."
    },
    {
      "id": "VIS-004",
      "severity": "release-blocking",
      "title": "Camera and lighting evidence still fails",
      "finding": "Every canonical below-hull quality frame is near-black; 20 deck frames are below 8% mean luminance; 44 of 370 quality frames are below 8% overall. Predator 57 and Manhattan 63 still have room cameras aimed into the exterior hull/sidewall. Superhawk's corrected room frames are no longer blank, but remain close-up blockouts and do not establish complete interiors.",
      "requiredAction": "Fix the below-hull and deck exposure, correct the two clipped room camera sets, and provide reviewable room framing with complete geometry."
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-001",
      "severity": "release-blocking",
      "title": "Interior LODs are unchanged",
      "finding": "Exterior LOD1 is lighter for 19 of 20 pairs, but Superhawk remains 13200 -> 13200 triangles. All 22 interior pairs retain the same triangle count; 16 are byte-identical and the remaining six differ in bytes without reducing triangles.",
      "requiredAction": "Produce genuinely lighter, visually acceptable interior LODs and a lighter Superhawk exterior LOD, then rerun parsed triangle and visual checks."
    },
    {
      "id": "APP-001",
      "severity": "release-blocking",
      "title": "No independent approval exists",
      "finding": "All 20 synchronized quality records remain changes-required with reviewer independent-qa-pending. All technical visual reviews remain pending, all publicationReady flags are false, and all metrics self-review statuses remain not QA-approved.",
      "requiredAction": "After the visual and LOD blockers are fixed, run a new independent QA pass and record explicit approval per selected ID."
    }
  ],
